      "summaries": {
        "en": "Pake is a command-line tool that converts any webpage into a lightweight desktop app using Rust and Tauri, avoiding Electron's bloat. It bundles a minimal browser view with the page, resulting in apps that are 10x smaller and use less memory. Ideal for wrapping web tools like ChatGPT, Claude, or Gemini into native-looking Mac, Windows, or Linux apps. Simply run `pake https://example.com` to generate a standalone executable.",
        "zh": "Pake 是基于 Rust 和 Tauri 的命令行工具，可将任意网页一键打包为轻量级桌面应用。它采用系统原生 WebView 渲染，相比 Electron 方案，安装包体积缩小 10 倍以上，内存占用更低。核心思路是用原生框架替代浏览器引擎，保留网页交互功能的同时，实现接近原生应用的启动速度与资源效率。用户只需执行 `pake https://example.com`，即可将 ChatGPT、Claude、Gemini 等网页工具快速生成为 Mac、Windows 或 Linux 可执行文件。适合频繁访问网页工具、避免浏览器标签干扰的场景，也便于开发者快速为 Web 项目生成桌面版本。",
        "es": "Pake is a command-line tool that converts any webpage into a lightweight desktop app using Rust and Tauri, avoiding Electron's bloat. It bundles a minimal browser view with the page, resulting in apps that are 10x smaller and use less memory. Ideal for wrapping web tools like ChatGPT, Claude, or Gemini into native-looking Mac, Windows, or Linux apps. Simply run `pake https://example.com` to generate a standalone executable.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "Pake stands out for chatgpt, claude, and desktop in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Pake is a command-line tool that converts any webpage into a lightweight desktop app using Rust and Tauri, avoiding Electron's bloat. It bundles a minimal browser view with the page, resulting in apps that are 10x smaller and use less memory. Ideal for wrapping web tools like ChatGPT, Claude, or Gemini into native-looking Mac, Windows, or Linux apps. Simply run `pake https://example.com` to generate a standalone executable.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/tw93/Pake for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
