      },
      "summaries": {
        "en": "Turso is an in-process SQL database that is fully compatible with SQLite, designed to solve latency and scaling issues in edge computing by leveraging libSQL and WebAssembly. Its key innovation is the ability to run SQLite in the browser or on edge functions via WASM, enabling low-latency, serverless data access. You can use Turso to build real-time apps with local-first data, replicate databases across edge locations, or embed it in mobile and desktop apps for offline-first experiences.",
        "zh": "Turso 是一个与 SQLite 完全兼容的进程内 SQL 数据库，专为解决边缘计算中的延迟和扩展问题而设计。其核心技术在于通过 libSQL 和 WebAssembly 将 SQLite 运行在浏览器或边缘函数中，实现低延迟的无服务器数据访问。你可以利用 Turso 构建实时应用，实现本地优先的数据管理，跨边缘位置复制数据库，或将其嵌入移动和桌面应用以获得离线优先体验。这一设计让开发者能够在边缘端直接处理数据，无需依赖远程服务器，从而大幅提升响应速度。",
        "es": "Turso is an in-process SQL database that is fully compatible with SQLite, designed to solve latency and scaling issues in edge computing by leveraging libSQL and WebAssembly. Its key innovation is the ability to run SQLite in the browser or on edge functions via WASM, enabling low-latency, serverless data access. You can use Turso to build real-time apps with local-first data, replicate databases across edge locations, or embed it in mobile and desktop apps for offline-first experiences.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "turso stands out for database, embedded-database, and sql in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Turso is an in-process SQL database that is fully compatible with SQLite, designed to solve latency and scaling issues in edge computing by leveraging libSQL and WebAssembly. Its key innovation is the ability to run SQLite in the browser or on edge functions via WASM, enabling low-latency, serverless data access. You can use Turso to build real-time apps with local-first data, replicate databases across edge locations, or embed it in mobile and desktop apps for offline-first experiences.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/tursodatabase/turso for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
